In the beginning, the world was shrouded in endless twilight. The Sun and Moon had not yet learned their dance, and darkness pressed heavily upon the earth. The people lived in fear, unable to see beyond their fires.

A young weaver named Celeste grew tired of the gloom. She gathered the finest silver threads from spider webs kissed by morning dew and began to weave. For seven days and seven nights, she worked without rest, creating a magnificent tapestry that shimmered with captured light.

When she finished, Celeste climbed to the highest mountain and threw her creation skyward with all her strength. The tapestry stretched and tore as it rose, scattering into countless glowing fragments across the heavens. Each piece became a star, burning with the light she had woven into every thread.

